Target Problem (your task):

\begin{theorem}\label{thm:sublinear}
    Let $\epsilon \leq 0.01$. For any choice of $\log^4 n \leq \Delta \leq n^\epsilon$, there is an $n$-vertex bipartite graph $G$ of maximum degree $\Delta$ such that any randomized algorithm that with probability at least $0.51$ provides a $(1, \epsilon n)$-approximation for the size of the maximum matching in $G$ must make $\Delta^{\Omega(1/\varepsilon)}$ adjacency list queries.
\end{theorem}

